Prompt:
I need to add clang-tools packaging to my package_tools.py script in my compendium-registry repo. The script already packages vcpkg. Now I need to add clang-tools that extracts a slim package from the full LLVM release.
Goal: Users who only need clang-tidy and clang-format shouldn't have to download the full 1.5GB LLVM tarball. The slim package should be ~50-100MB.
What to extract from the LLVM tarball:
Binaries:

bin/clang-tidy
bin/clang-format
bin/clang-apply-replacements

Shared libraries (if needed — check with ldd on Linux / otool -L on macOS):

Any libs from lib/ that these binaries depend on
On macOS, these may be statically linked already

Platform matrix:

linux-amd64: LLVM-{version}-Linux-X64.tar.xz
linux-arm64: LLVM-{version}-Linux-ARM64.tar.xz
darwin-arm64: LLVM-{version}-macOS-ARM64.tar.xz

Source: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases
Output per platform:

clang-tools-{version}-{os}-{arch}.tar.gz
Extracts as clang-tools/bin/clang-tidy, clang-tools/bin/clang-format, etc.
SHA256 checksum

Important notes:

This can run from one machine for all platforms — download, extract specific files, repackage
On Linux, the binaries may need lib/libclang-cpp.so and lib/libLLVM.so — check dependencies
On macOS, binaries may be self-contained — verify with otool -L
The full LLVM tarball is ~1.5GB per platform, so download once per platform, extract what we need, delete the rest
Follow the same pattern as the vcpkg packager in package_tools.py

Registry manifest entry should look like:
json"clang-tools": {
  "22.1.2": {
    "linux": {
      "amd64": {
        "url": "https://github.com/ileanmjr88/compendium-registry/releases/download/v0.1.0/clang-tools-22.1.2-linux-amd64.tar.gz",
        "checksum": "sha256:...",
        "size": ...,
        "strip": 1
      }
    }
  }
}
The existing package_tools.py is attached. Add the package_clang_tools() function following the same pattern as package_vcpkg().